{
  "mn9:0.1": "Middle Discourses 9 ",
  "mn9:0.2": "Right View ",
  "mn9:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn9:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn9:1.3": "There Sāriputta addressed the mendicants: ",
  "mn9:1.4": "“Reverends, mendicants!” ",
  "mn9:1.5": "“Reverend,” they replied. ",
  "mn9:1.6": "Sāriputta said this: ",
  "mn9:2.1": "“Reverends, they speak of this thing called ‘right view’. ",
  "mn9:2.2": "How do you define a noble disciple who has right view, whose view is correct, who has experiential confidence in the teaching, and has come to the true teaching?” ",
  "mn9:2.3": "“Reverend, we would travel a long way to learn the meaning of this statement in the presence of Venerable Sāriputta. ",
  "mn9:2.4": "May Venerable Sāriputta himself please clarify the meaning of this. ",
  "mn9:2.5": "The mendicants will listen and remember it.” ",
  "mn9:2.6": "“Well then, reverends, listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "mn9:2.7": "“Yes, reverend,” they replied. ",
  "mn9:2.8": "Sāriputta said this: ",
  "mn9:3.1": "“A noble disciple understands the unskillful and its root, and the skillful and its root. ",
  "mn9:3.2": "When they’ve done this, they’re defined as a noble disciple who has right view, whose view is correct, who has experiential confidence in the teaching, and has come to the true teaching. ",
  "mn9:4.1": "But what is the unskillful and what is its root? And what 